course: dictionary
lesson: 4231
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word grand is one of them. To find the right meaning, read the sentence around it. Those words are its context, and they give you clues.
explain: «The castle had a grand hall with tall pillars.» Here grand means big and splendid, because a hall with tall pillars is impressive. Try the meaning in the sentence: big and splendid hall. It still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: «That's grand, thanks.» In Ireland and the UK, people use grand in this everyday way to mean fine or OK. «It cost five grand» is different: grand here is slang for a thousand pounds, so five grand is five thousand pounds. The number before it is your clue.
explain: Grand also appears in grandmother and grandson. There it means one generation further, so your grandmother is your parent's mother. When you meet a word you know in a new place, check the context before you decide what it means.
fact: Grand means big, impressive and splendid, like a grand palace.
fact: Grand can also mean important or proud.
fact: In Ireland and the UK, «That's grand» is an informal way to say fine or OK.
fact: A grand is slang for a thousand pounds or dollars, so «five grand» means five thousand.
fact: In grandmother and grandson, grand means one generation further, and a grand total is the final total of everything.
exercise: «The castle had a grand hall with tall pillars.» What does grand mean here? | *Big and splendid | Full of noise | Very small | Cold and damp
exercise: Ciara is asked if she wants more tea and says, «That's grand, thanks.» What does grand mean? | A thousand cups | Tall and thin | *Fine, or OK | Very rich
exercise: «The new car cost five grand.» What does grand mean here? | *A thousand pounds | A very grand palace | Five cars | A big family
test: «The grand finale of the show was a firework display.» What does grand mean in the phrase grand finale? | Wet and grey | *Big and splendid, the best part | Sleepy and slow | Small and quiet
test: In the word grandmother, what does grand mean? | Important and proud | A thousand | Very old | *One generation further back
exam: «Her grand total came to two hundred pounds.» What does grand total mean? | A total that is grand, like a palace | *The final total of everything | A secret number | A very big pile of coins
